<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47339" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tābĭfĭcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>melting</i>, <i>dissolving</i>, <i>wasting</i>, <i>infectious</i>, <i>corroding</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radii (solis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					6, 737</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venenum lentum atque tabificum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 73</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seps,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					9, 723</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aër,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 5,
					911</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 37, 56, § 134</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					6, 276</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caeli vitia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Oedip. 79</span></i>
			: terram edisse his tabificum est, <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 10,
				10, § 29</span></i>: tabificae mentis perturbationes,
			* <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 4, 16, 36</span></i>.</div>
